Horologium Schranz

Ingredients: HARDCORE TECHNO / RAVE + SYMPHONIC & GOTHIC METAL + TRIPPY, SURREAL & PSYCHEDELIC + Trombone  
Creative Catalyst: Instrument bodies forged from iron-nickel meteorite fragments and internally fitted with self-winding antique clockwork mechanics.

A terrifying, ecstasy-drenched assault where 200 BPM gabber kickdrums are hand-cranked through brass escapements, and operatic gothic dirges are bent through Doppler-shifting brass bells. Deep, guttural brass roars act as the principal bassline, tearing through layers of hallucinogenic, pitch-shifted choral swells and heavy metallic guitar chugging. The result sounds like a cathedral-sized grandfather clock detonating inside an underground warehouse party, folding time in on itself with brutal, psychedelic precision.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 185–210 BPM. A relentlessly hammering, unyielding 4-on-the-floor kick pattern intersected by syncopated, mechanical clockwork ticks and sliding brass accents.
- Harmonic Palette: Phrygian Dominant and Harmonic Minor scales, drenched in microtonal detuning caused by the unpredictable thermal expanding of space-iron.
- Production Signatures: Brass-Formant Distortion (running low-register trombone slides directly into overdriven vacuum-tube guitar stacks), Doppler-Bending Reverberation (simulating room reflections that expand and contract in pitch with timekeeping gears), and Stutter-Chop Poly-Rhythms (triggering high-speed rave stabs synced to mechanical escapement gear teeth).
- Dynamics: Extreme, violent shifts. Track construction alternates instantly between massive, suffocating walls of symphonic brass violence and silent, ticking suspense where only a solitary, trippy vocal echo remains.

